# INTENTIONALLY EMPTY - no LineageEmitter is registered by this module.
#
# DataCatalogLineageEmitter used to be listed here. It was removed in
# sprint-23 (Story 1.5) for two independent reasons:
#
#  1. NOT CONSTRUCTIBLE. Its only constructor takes three arguments
#     (client, entryName, tagTemplate), so ServiceLoader raised
#     ServiceConfigurationError on every discovery pass. AutoConfig
#     swallowed that error (AutoConfig.java:227), truncating the provider
#     list, and DefaultRuntimeContext.java:276 then substituted
#     NoOpDefaults.NoOpLineageEmitter. The registration therefore
#     advertised an emitter that never emitted - silently.
#
#  2. DEAD BACKEND. It writes com.google.cloud.datacatalog.v1 Tags, and
#     Data Catalog entered its phased shutdown on 2026-06-01. Lineage has
#     since moved to the Data Lineage API (datalineage.googleapis.com,
#     Java client google-cloud-datalineage).
#
# Removing the line is behaviour-identical to the swallowed error it
# replaces - discovery still yields no LineageEmitter, and the runtime
# still falls back to the no-op - but it no longer advertises a lie, and
# it satisfies Story 1.2 AC 3.
#
# The class itself is retained (deprecated) for callers that construct it
# explicitly against a project where Data Catalog still answers. Re-listing
# it here is NOT the fix: a working no-arg constructor over a shut-down API
# would turn today's silent no-op into a runtime failure.
#
# Re-register a replacement here once the Data Lineage API adapter exists.
# That migration is blocked offline: google-cloud-datalineage is absent
# from ~/.m2 (only google-cloud-datalineage-bom poms are cached), and this
# build runs with `mvn -o`. Tracked by Story 1.5 AC 2 / AC 5.
